.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man8/kbdrate.8, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt KBDRATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kbdrate
.Nd set the keyboard repeat rate and delay
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl d Ar milliseconds
.Op Fl r Ar rate
.Op Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sets the delay before a held key repeats and the repeat rate in characters
per second.
It first uses KDKBDREP on descriptor 0.
On Rach2, redirect input from
.Pa /dev/console
when running it through SSH or a terminal emulator.
.Pp
The default delay is 250 milliseconds and the default rate is 10.9
characters per second.
A successful KDKBDREP request reports the actual delay and rate.
If the console refuses KDKBDREP, the upstream program attempts other
hardware interfaces, including
.Pa /dev/port ,
which Rach2 does not provide.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d Ar milliseconds
Set the delay before repeats start.
.It Fl r Ar rate
Set the repeats per second.
.It Fl s
Suppress the result message.
.It Fl h
Print help.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kbdrate -d 250 -r 30 < /dev/console
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr setleds 1 ,
.Xr vconsole.conf 5
